Subject: [PATCH 13/16] ttf: name the glyphs of a font that has no glyph names

A format 3 post table names no glyph, and the names are synthesized as gidN,
so glyph 0 came out as gid0 and a compiler added a .notdef of its own in
front of it. Glyph 0 is now .notdef and an encoded glyph is named for its
codepoint as the Adobe Glyph List Specification does (uniXXXX, uXXXXX),
through RenameGlyphs, so components, kerning and features follow.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
